  "status": "Complete: exact fused quantized row pairs, exact/reference checks, one Inkling timing and shared-engine regression passed",
  "implementation": [
    "Replace separate vmulpd/vaddpd with vfmadd231pd in existing two-row/four-vector and two-row/six-vector dot kernels",
    "For finite binary32 multiplicands widened to binary64, each nonzero product needs at most 48 significand bits and has magnitude >=2^-298 and <2^256; binary64 represents the product exactly, so FMA and separate multiplication/addition round only the same addition",
    "Keep the original per-output four-lane order and 2048-element span folds; no reassociation or compiler fast-math change",
    "Use the existing Wide_Halves/x86-64-v3 CPU guard, which already requires CPUID FMA and OS XMM/YMM state",
    "Keep single-vector dots, dispatch, weight storage and buffers unchanged; no new runtime, threads or persistent allocations"
  ],
  "changed_source_files": [
    "src/library/model_runner-tensors.adb",
    "tests/src/tests-gguf_cases.adb"
  ],
  "focused_aunit": {
    "gguf_and_kernels": "81/81",
    "native_inkling": "15/15"
  },
  "exact_test": "Existing five-format old-row/paired-row bitwise tests cover counts 1\u201315/31/32/33/127/128/129, row ranges, shifted bounds, unaligned weights and untouched outputs. New Q8_0 cases compare paired FMA to scalar separate multiply/add with maximum/minimum finite binary32 values, subnormals, cancellation, signed-zero-only vectors, 256/2048/2304-column spans and counts 4/5/6/7/8/9/12/13/16. Quantization.Use_Wide_Decoders is disabled for the new scalar reference.",
  "equivalence_domain": "Finite binary32 multiplicands; arbitrary binary64 products do not have this guarantee. No NaN payload equivalence claim is made.",
